## Context

§3 of `slides/manuscript/main.md` ("Third, from chatbots to knowledge
management", lines 40–51 pre-edit) is currently an embryo: six
"limits" enumerated (articulation, coverage, reasoning, tool-use,
retroactivity, agency) with three of them stubbed (`—.`), followed by
a one-paragraph industry trajectory narrative. It needs a rewrite.

## Author directive (2026-05-21, verbatim)

> Section 3 is embryo. Open a ticket to sweep existing contents (see
> previous line) and propose a page. We made empirical research, had a
> timeline. Do NOT try to defend the mapping of quality <-> industry
> stages. Quality axes are ordered, and even within an axis it is
> simplifying to think of it as a ladder. Better think of it as a
> spider graph (aside: we will probably need such a graph to grade the
> reports quality. I hope there is a ticket already open for quality
> judgment). The industry is pushing the enveloppe not climbing a
> ladder. Agent capabilities improve statistical dataset quality. Do
> we need a heatmap or a flow chart ?

## Constraints (load-bearing)

- **No defense of a quality↔stages mapping.** The current §3 implicitly
  maps each capability (articulation, coverage, reasoning, …) onto a
  §2 quality dimension. Drop that mapping. It is not the claim.
- **Quality axes are ordered but not ladders.** Within accuracy /
  coherence / provenance / temporality, "ladder" oversimplifies. Use
  spider-graph framing instead — each axis a separate ray, joint
  performance an enclosed shape.
- **Industry pushes the envelope, not climbs a ladder.** The §3
  narrative is about the outer surface of what is commercially
  attainable expanding over time, not about labs climbing the same
  staircase.
- **One-sentence thesis.** Agent capabilities improve statistical
  dataset quality. That is the claim §3 should land.

## Sweep targets (read all before proposing)

- `slides/manuscript/main.md` §3 (current state)
- `docs/capability-timeline.md` (empirical chronology, four-lab matrix)
- `docs/related-work/03-capability-ladder.md` (15-citation due-diligence note)
- `report/report.tex` (esp. the capability-history sections, French
  prose, and existing citations)
- `slides/slides.tex` (the talk version of the same argument)
- Tickets 0146 (capability-timeline expand + figure — sweep-skipped
  twice as scope-too-large), 0152 (align-slides-on-argument),
  0144 (RAG/reasoning/coherence-cell)

## Open visualization question

Heatmap vs flowchart vs spider-graph montage? Possibilities:

- **Heatmap** — labs × capability-stage × time-of-arrival. Reads as
  "the envelope advances across the industry," not "this lab is
  ahead."
- **Flowchart / DAG** — capabilities as nodes, dependencies as edges
  (1→2 sequential; 3+4 parallel and merging into 5; 5→6→7). Reads as
  "these capabilities have a structural ordering" without claiming a
  performance ladder.
- **Spider-graph montage** — one spider per generation of agents,
  showing the joint accuracy/coherence/provenance/temporality
  envelope expanding over time. Reads as "the achievable quality
  surface grows."
- **Combination** — heatmap or DAG for the capability surface, spider
  graph for the quality surface.

The proposal should pick one (or none), with rationale.

## Related open tickets

- **0201** — Quality composite axis (coherence/provenance/temporality
  scorers). This is the ticket the author refers to as "quality
  judgment". The spider-graph-for-grading concern is already covered
  there; this §3 ticket does not duplicate scope. If §3 lands a
  spider-graph figure, the figure-generation script likely lives
  next to whatever 0201 produces.
- **0146** — Capability timeline expansion + figure. Has the data
  substrate (seven-stage matrix, ≥4 labs). The proposal here may
  share or refactor that figure.
- **0199** — Experiment 2 spec/run. The §4 result will eventually
  push the §3 envelope; the §3 page should land before Exp 2 results
