## Actions

1. Read all sweep targets end-to-end. Take notes.
2. Draft a §3 proposal as a single self-contained page (max ≈ 1.5
   pages rendered) that obeys the four constraints above. Save the
   draft to `docs/section3-proposal.md` for review before touching
   `slides/manuscript/main.md`.
3. Pick a visualization mode (heatmap / flowchart / spider / none)
   with a one-paragraph rationale.
4. List the citations the rewrite will need; cross-check against
   `report/refs.bib` and `docs/related-work/03-capability-ladder.md`.
5. After author sign-off on the proposal, write the §3 prose to
   `slides/manuscript/main.md` and wire any new figure into the
   Makefile per the figures-are-artifacts rule.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `docs/section3-proposal.md` exists, ≤ 1.5 rendered pages.
- [ ] Proposal answers the heatmap-vs-flowchart-vs-spider question
      with rationale.
- [ ] Author has approved the proposal (log entry on this ticket).
- [ ] `slides/manuscript/main.md` §3 replaced.
- [ ] Any new figure has a Makefile target and renders cleanly via
      `pandoc slides/manuscript/main.md -o main.pdf
      --pdf-engine=tectonic --resource-path=slides`.
- [ ] No paragraph in §3 defends a quality↔stages mapping.
- [ ] One-sentence thesis "agent capabilities improve statistical
      dataset quality" appears explicitly in the rewrite.
